        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: तजुर्बा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तजुर्बा — tajurbā — \"experience (gained over time)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अरुण को इस काम का दस साल का तजुर्बा है। Aruṇ ko is kām kā das sāl kā tajurbā hai. Arun has ten years' experience of this work."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तजुर्बा (tajurbā) is usually traced to Arabic tajriba, \"a trial, a test\", through Persian; Hindi uses it for what years of doing something teach you."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
